                  <provenance type="#i" source="2931"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_224">Glastonbury, Somerset.
                        Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>"Libellus ffratris
                        Iohannis Merylynch. de perquisito eiusdem" (fols. 48v, 57v, 58r, 66v,
                        67r).</p><p>"Liber Roberti [...]" (fol. 1r), s. xv.</p><p>"Glastonia" (fol.
                        49r, in red ink).</p><p>List of abbots of Glastonbury on fols. 181v, 182r in
                        one hand to John Chinnock (d. 1420) and in another to Richard Whiting, the
                        last abbot.</p><p>In double cols. of 50 lines as Harley 641 fols. 118--206,
                        and Harley 651 fols. 185--191.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Binding with arms of Sir Symonds d'Ewes.
                     D'Ewe's title page and foliation.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"vol. sive tomus 61." ? = d'Ewes 107 (9967)
                     in CMA.</provenance>
               <provenance cert="low" source="8547"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_439">Oxford, Oxfordshire. The Queen's
                        College</orgName><p>It is suggested that this, a Glastonbury book, was
                        that seen by Bale (Index, 6) at Queen’s. It was acquired (or re-acquired) by
                        the college c. 1700. See Kidd, The Queen’s College, 130 and CBLMC 16, 1235.
                        The case appears a doubtful one.</p><p>See also under
                     Glastonbury</p></provenance>
               </history>
